.TH DISK-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-19" "disk-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
disk-revamped \- usage, free space and fill rate in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B disk-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B disk-revamped
shows how full a disk is in the tmux status line, with its used, free and total space, the inode usage, the read and write rates, the fill rate and the time until full, a graph of the recent readings, the purgeable space on macOS, and a list of every real disk or of the mounts you name. The usage comes from
.B df \-Pk
on both systems, through
.B /bin/df
on macOS, so GNU coreutils first on PATH does not change it.
.PP
The entry point
.B disk-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup keys in one tmux call and replaces the placeholders #{disk_percentage}, #{disk_icon}, #{disk_fg_color}, #{disk_bg_color}, #{disk_used}, #{disk_total}, #{disk_free}, #{disk_read}, #{disk_write}, #{disk_all}, #{disk_inodes}, #{disk_purgeable}, #{disk_graph}, #{disk_fill_rate}, #{disk_full_eta} and #{disk_mounts} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When the reading is older than the interval it starts one in the background, so the status line never waits. The inodes, the purgeable space, the fill rate, the mounts and the per-disk rates are read only for a placeholder the status line uses. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a menu.
.PP
The read and write rates come from /proc/diskstats on Linux, summed over the whole devices in /sys/block, and compare each reading with the one before it; macOS has no such counters, so they stay empty there. The purgeable space comes from diskutil on macOS and is empty on Linux.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the popup keys and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored reading: percentage, icon, fg_color, bg_color, used, total, read, write, all, free, inodes, purgeable, graph, fill_rate, full_eta, mounts. The status line runs it, and it starts a reading in the background when the stored one is older than the interval. A name that is none of them prints nothing.
.TP
.B refresh
Read the disk now, read the details the status line uses, store the reading and say how full the disk is.
.TP
.B card
Read everything now and print one row per figure, then every disk, cut to the rows and the width of the terminal it runs in.
.TP
.B scan
List the largest items under the scanned path, with their sizes, biggest first, dot entries included. A scan stays fresh for the scan interval.
.TP
.B popup
Open the card in a tmux popup, which Enter closes. The popup key runs it. A tmux older than 3.2 says so.
.TP
.B eat
Open the scan in a tmux popup, which Enter closes. The eat key runs it.
.TP
.B daemon
Read the disk and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per interval, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the popups, df, each tool or file a figure comes from, the terminal size, the notifier, the settings, the keys it found bound, gum and the core tools.
.br
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
.br
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-fill\-rate\-label .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the popup keys and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI DISK_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR DISK_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option, and an empty value is used as given.
.TP
.B DISK_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B DISK_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B DISK_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B DISK_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the detail popup. off binds nothing. The default is M\-d, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_eat_key
The prefix key that opens the largest items popup. off or empty binds nothing. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_mount
The mount the usage placeholders report. The default is /. On macOS / is the sealed system volume, so /System/Volumes/Data shows the space your files use.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_mounts
The mounts #{disk_mounts} lists, separated by spaces or commas. A mount that does not exist is left out. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_interval
Seconds a reading stays fresh before df is run again. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_detail_interval
Seconds the list of every disk stays fresh. The default is 60.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_render
jobs turns each placeholder into a call the status line runs. options turns it into a read of a tmux option that the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. Any other value means jobs. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_history_length
How many readings #{disk_graph} keeps. The default is 20.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_notify
1 sends a desktop notification when the usage reaches the high threshold, and again after it has fallen below it. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_medium_thresh
Usage percent at which the tier becomes medium. The default is 70.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_high_thresh
Usage percent at which the tier becomes high, and at which a notification is sent. The default is 90.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_low_icon
What #{disk_icon} prints in the low tier. The default is one bar of three.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_medium_icon
What #{disk_icon} prints in the medium tier. The default is two bars of three.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_high_icon
What #{disk_icon} prints in the high tier. The default is three bars.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_low_fg_color
The style #{disk_fg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_medium_fg_color
The style #{disk_fg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_high_fg_color
The style #{disk_fg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_low_bg_color
The style #{disk_bg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_medium_bg_color
The style #{disk_bg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_high_bg_color
The style #{disk_bg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_percentage_format
printf format of #{disk_percentage}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_size_format
printf format of a size below 1024G; from 1024G a size is terabytes with one decimal, such as 1.8T. The default is %sG.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_inodes_format
printf format of #{disk_inodes}. The default is i%s%%.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_separator
Text between disks in #{disk_all} and #{disk_mounts}. The default is a comma and a space.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_icons
ascii labels nothing. nerd puts a Nerd Font glyph before every metric that takes a label. The default is ascii.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_fixed_width
on pads each figure on the left to its natural width, so a change from 9% to 42% does not shift the status line. The default is off.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_percentage_label
Text printed before the usage, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_used_label
Text printed before the used space, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_total_label
Text printed before the total space, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_free_label
Text printed before the free space, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_read_label
Text printed before the read rate, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_write_label
Text printed before the write rate, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_inodes_label
Text printed before the inode usage, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_purgeable_label
Text printed before the purgeable space, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_graph_label
Text printed before the graph, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_fill_rate_label
Text printed before the fill rate, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_full_eta_label
Text printed before the time until full, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_mounts_label
Text printed before the list of your mounts, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_all_label
Text printed before the list of every disk, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_percentage_width
Characters the usage is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_used_width
Characters the used space is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_total_width
Characters the total space is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_free_width
Characters the free space is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_read_width
Characters the read rate is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_write_width
Characters the write rate is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_inodes_width
Characters the inode usage is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_purgeable_width
Characters the purgeable space is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_graph_width
Characters the graph is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_fill_rate_width
Characters the fill rate is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_full_eta_width
Characters the time until full is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_mounts_width
Characters the list of your mounts is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_all_width
Characters the list of every disk is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_eat_path
The folder the largest items popup and scan list. The default is the mount.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_eat_count
How many of the largest items the scan lists. The default is 10.
.TP
.B @disk_revamped_eat_interval
Seconds a scan result stays fresh. The default is 60.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored reading lives in
.BR @disk_revamped_percent ,
.BR _used ,
.BR _total ,
.BR _free ,
.BR _inodes ,
.BR _purgeable ,
.BR _read ,
.BR _write ,
.BR _fill_rate ,
.BR _full_eta ,
.BR _all ,
.BR _mounts_list ,
.BR _history
and
.BR _eat ,
with the time of each reading in options that end in _ts. apply records the placeholders the status line uses in
.BR @disk_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @disk_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @disk_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR du (1),
.BR diskutil (8),
.BR gum (1)
